-- title:
--   Trivial residue action at supersingular points of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$, and $K_1$ the $L$-subfield generated likewise by the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, with $K_1 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ and $K_1$ compatibly, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal. Let $j \in K$ and $j_1 \in K_1$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent series is the $q$-expansion of $j$, and let $\iota_F$ be an $A$-algebra map from the chart algebra of $K_1$ (elements of $K_1$ integral over $A[j_1]$) to that of $K$ (elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) inducing the identity on Laurent series. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra of $K$ whose prime ideal contains the image of $\varpi$ and is supersingular, in the sense that for every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ with kernel exactly $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$: every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $p$. Finally let $G$ be a finite group acting on $K$ by ring automorphisms over $L$ whose fixed field is exactly $K_1$ (every $g$ fixes elements of $K$ lying in $K_1$, and elements fixed by all of $G$ lie in $K_1$), with a compatible action on the chart algebra of $K$. Then for every $g \in G$ stabilising the prime ideal of $y$ and every $b$ in the chart algebra of $K$, one has $g \cdot b - b \in y$.
--
--   This is the statement that at a supersingular point of the stable model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$, lying above the floor $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$, the decomposition group of the covering coincides with the inertia group: a Galois element fixing the point acts trivially on its residue ring, reflecting the total ramification of the Igusa covering at supersingular points. It feeds the construction of elements of the chart algebra with prescribed behaviour at $y$ in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_exists_sub_mem_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_exists_sub_mem_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul).
